    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a heavy way to put it. \"no longer fighting for anything\"... it kind of makes the whole climb feel like a waste of time. if the prize at the end is just this void, what was the point of all the stress and the sacrifices? it feels like i've just finished a marathon only to find out there's nowhere to go after the finish line. it's just... quiet. and exhausting.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
